INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('ac763ea0-5b70-4fac-9763-b228ad0df825','164d01e6-c6d8-4290-b4dc-8337aeabf286','google:Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25JeU5YQTNTbUZoUW0xVE0xcDVOMFpIVW5KMVRtYxAB','google','The Gambini pasta is delicious!',5,'2026-10-08','2026-11-12T15:36:35.256Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('34f373e5-151b-492b-9e7d-a585bdbd0649','164d01e6-c6d8-4290-b4dc-8337aeabf286','google:Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2taclJHRnpiMmx2Y2xKcFNHaFFVSGQzVDJ4eldVRRAB','google','Nice local watering hole, with decent faire that is a step or two above chains but isnt going to win any awards. Family friendly with plenty of seating for large parties, bar side has many televisions and hosts sporting events regularly. Great service all around.',5,'2026-09-29','2026-11-12T15:36:35.256Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('54e826b8-17f8-404d-852e-2bc688e62e28','164d01e6-c6d8-4290-b4dc-8337aeabf286','google:Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT201alNsQXlkemcwT1dodmJYZFBNakF5TW1SRVlWRRAB','google','Food was decent. We had a large group. 12 total with 5 of those being kids. Meals came out sporadically.  My husband''s didn''t come out for 38 minutes. They came and apologized and comped that which was nice.  No water refills,  no checking in,  there were tables around us so we weren''t that hard to see to ask if we were good. They just didn''t.',3,'2026-09-21','2026-11-12T15:36:35.256Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('0e5008e1-7175-4ce9-bbe3-d79fe02684af','164d01e6-c6d8-4290-b4dc-8337aeabf286','google:Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21GeU9HZEVPVzFETkV0blJIZzBZa1E1YVc5aloyYxAB','google','We went for a work event and we got free buffet! It was the my first time visiting, and the atmosphere was great!',4,'2026-09-19','2026-11-12T15:36:35.256Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('34022198-b4c1-4333-a00d-2d3e28db285f','164d01e6-c6d8-4290-b4dc-8337aeabf286','google:Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21WS2FsVmhNbU5wUzFsblFrSm5lbFJEVWxZMGQxRRAB','google','Was on way to hotel and glad we stopped. Good range of available food. And beer of course.  Haha',5,'2026-09-19','2026-11-12T15:36:35.256Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('93d9d8fd-0d89-4d03-8d35-7d2e2eb63874','164d01e6-c6d8-4290-b4dc-8337aeabf286','google:Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT25FMWJtMHpkSFppZG1oaGFsUllNbUpUZGpoRVNFRRAB','google','Since this is a tap house, temper expectations accordingly as it does fit that level of “pub food” quality. It was Sunday, so there were a few tables of NFL football fans. However, it wasn’t overly crowded, and even with their enthusiasm or expressions of disappointment (LOL), it wasn’t that noisy.<br><br>The food: The Maverick Burger (ordered without a bun) is a disappointment. It’s obviously a frozen hamburger patty with some cheese and bacon on it. It wasn’t very flavorful without the barbecue sauce, which we ordered on the side. The onion rings were almost inedible. First, they were completely cold. Then the breading on them is so hard, it will scratch the roof of the mouth. The onion inside is so overcooked that it was shriveled into a shoe string like shape. Plus, the flavor Isn’t appealing at all. The menu says that jicama slaw comes with the burger, but that did not appear. We didn’t ask, because the rest of the plate was so unsatisfying. The Timberwood fries were the best part, even though they are certainly frozen fries from a bag. They’re battered and cooked perfectly.<br><br>The other choice was the wings. They are certainly better than BWW‘s. Highly recommend the Memphis dry rub. The wings were cooked appropriately and the seasoning on them wasn’t overdone. Great pub food choice!<br><br>Our waiter’s name was Wyatt, and he was a kind and attentive young man who shared a smile. We never had to ask for drink refills, and he checked on us periodically without being too frequent. Maybe ask for him as your waiter when you visit.<br><br>There was one thing we noticed — none of the employees were smiling (with the exception of Wyatt while we chatted with him at our table). We kept waiting for it throughout our entire experience, and we just kept noticing the sour expressions and downcast looks. Everyone seemed either really stressed or really sad. It wasn’t extremely busy when we were there, so we are wondering if management is good to its employees… is it a good place to work? It didn’t look like anyone in uniform wanted to be there. We felt kinda sad for them. :-(',3,'2026-09-15','2026-11-12T15:36:35.256Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('fe2c515b-0519-42bb-af48-0aa6739ab766','164d01e6-c6d8-4290-b4dc-8337aeabf286','google:Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2pSVk5FRnFObTlMUVRoWVJucEtVVzlpUVRkUVJWRRAB','google','Great atmosphere, great service, great food. Had Steak Salad and Shrimp Gambini... Both delicious.',5,'2026-09-15','2026-11-12T15:36:35.256Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('b041027c-852b-43e1-8bbc-4cbd29bf9059','164d01e6-c6d8-4290-b4dc-8337aeabf286','google:Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xsb2RIVnpVVTV5VTJ0dWNrOXRla2hvUkcxS2RGRRAB','google','It’s been a long time since I’ve been truly blown away by exceptional customer service, but the staff and management at Timberwood made such an impression on me that I’m writing this review three months after our visit!<br>Two friends and I chose Timberwood for a birthday dinner for our friend (on or around June 11), who absolutely loves their burgers (the Clint Eastwood, I think!). As usual, her burger was delicious. Unfortunately, the calamari I ordered was another story. I’m still not sure what chemical reaction or cooking time could possibly turn fried calamari into shriveled-up, tiny, stale Funyuns, but that’s essentially what I was served. 😂<br><br>I felt terrible having to send it back, but even our waitress agreed that it was inedible. What happened next, though, is exactly why I’m giving Timberwood near 5th street such a high rating. Not only did they immediately make things right by letting me order something else and sincerely apologizing, but later, when our table was suddenly under a cloud of cigarette smoke thanks to some random and inconsiderate guy, the manager came out personally to address the situation. He reassured us, apologized, and made sure we were taken care of.<br><br>My replacement meal was amazing, our bill was discounted, and our birthday girl received a delicious birthday treat. A lot went wrong that evening, but so much more went right.<br><br>That kind of service makes all the difference and it''s so sparse these days. We already visit Timberwood often, and we’ll definitely keep going, especially when the staff and management care this much about their customers... next time, I’ll just stick with the fish and chips or my new favorite, the patty melt!<br><br>Wonderful server, wonderful management, and wonderful customer service!',5,'2026-09-14','2026-11-12T15:36:35.256Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('12c53bc6-ffc7-4581-a520-1ad6263f3b50','164d01e6-c6d8-4290-b4dc-8337aeabf286','google:Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21OMFRHVndhR0ZWYkdSWlMxWjFiMFZzVkhwbWRFRRAB','google','Well ordered a side of bacon 🥓 bacon came hard as a rock an cold asked for different bacon that wasnt hard an cold was told they dont cook bacon except in the mornings an its used for the entire day, I know some like cold crispy bacon but not everyone, also I couldn''t order the enchiladas with no peppers as they are also pre made in the mornings an not made to order yea pretty sure this will be my last visit',1,'2026-09-12','2026-11-12T15:36:35.256Z');
