INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('2378db39-8977-44ad-99d9-a05a7eeb3077','3c59354c-78be-4335-ac27-a27ff4cce713','google:ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURyZzctS1pREAE','google','The woman at the front of the restaurant was extremely rude.',1,'2024-07-19','2026-11-12T15:37:09.035Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('074e0d6c-ae2c-40ee-92b5-1e2ea5c42c43','3c59354c-78be-4335-ac27-a27ff4cce713','google:ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNweVk3Tl9BRRAB','google','I''m obsessed with their Pizza they are the best pizza joint here in Charlottesville. But I ordered today and I asked for some oregano and they charged me $1 for a small amount of oregano and that makes me disappointed. Not for the money I paid but its just a flake i didn''t ask for a side',5,'2024-07-11','2026-11-12T15:37:09.035Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('097db371-899d-4548-99a7-216b673abaca','3c59354c-78be-4335-ac27-a27ff4cce713','google:ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNyOE42c2dBRRAB','google','Very efficient takeout window. You can either order ahead or at the window. Food is ready in 10 minutes. We had the margherita pizza, porchetta sandwich, cheesy bread, and Brussels sprouts salad. Everything was delicious! The sandwich reminded us of the ones we ate when we were in Italy.',5,'2024-07-03','2026-11-12T15:37:09.035Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('c1ef4d60-f5dc-48a8-b24d-8badbcf6167a','3c59354c-78be-4335-ac27-a27ff4cce713','google:ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUREenMyZkl3EAE','google','We got a carry out from Lampo''s XPark location, and we sorely disappointed in the pizzas (Marguerita and the one with  prosciutto and arugula) compared to these same pizzas before Lampo was sold. They were dry, leathery and the prosciutto wasn''t prosciutto. Their eat-in location may have better pizzas and other food because they still have a lot of customers. Their Bar with outdoor music is popular and the music so far this season has been great!',3,'2024-04-09','2026-11-12T15:37:09.035Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('87b88c7d-4690-40fa-a110-ad0498f8bdab','3c59354c-78be-4335-ac27-a27ff4cce713','google:ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUQ5LTVtLTNRRRAB','google','I recently tried Lampo2Go, a takeout-only pizza place. My experience was a mix of good and bad. I''m passionate about good food and more so a believer in the seemingly dying commitment to good service, so I wanted to share my thoughts on this experience. I''ll be polite and honest to help both the restaurant and future customers.<br><br>Food Quality: The best thing I tried was the panouzzi polpettini. It looked great and tasted good, but it wasn''t hot. This made a big difference because the cheese didn''t melt, and the flavors weren''t as strong as they could have been. It was disappointing because it could have been much better.<br><br>Service: The staff were friendly, but they forgot to give me napkins. This might seem small, but it shows that they weren''t paying attention to details. I didn''t say anything because I thought they should know to give napkins without being told.<br><br>Price: The sandwich cost over $18, which is a lot. I expected something great, but it wasn''t worth the cost. The idea of Lampo2Go is interesting, but the food and service need to be better for the price.<br><br>Overall, Lampo2Go has potential, but it needs to improve. The idea of a takeout-only place is cool, but they need to make sure the food is hot, and they give customers what they need. I might go back, but only if they improve.',3,'2024-03-21','2026-11-12T15:37:09.035Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('7e3330f1-008a-4de0-82f8-bff8898b1ad7','3c59354c-78be-4335-ac27-a27ff4cce713','google:ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNOb3BUNWhBRRAB','google','We love Lampo but have been burned by Lampo2Go two times in a row now. The pizzas were very under sauced and were like eating soft and cold bread, not hot and crisp pizza like at the restaurant. We picked it up about 10 minutes before our estimated time too, hoping to catch them fresh out of the oven, but they were already in a waiting oven to keep warm. We expect more, especially considering they’ve bumped the prices about 40% in the past few years.',3,'2024-01-13','2026-11-12T15:37:09.035Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('042123fb-ad31-4484-aed9-b3dbd8fca31b','3c59354c-78be-4335-ac27-a27ff4cce713','google:ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURGNTRpVkhnEAE','google','Efficient order-ahead spot for carry out Italian style pizza - just as good as their sit down restaurant',5,'2023-11-11','2026-11-12T15:37:09.035Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('aac81755-248d-41c6-a28e-f309a0fe9177','3c59354c-78be-4335-ac27-a27ff4cce713','google:ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURaeVpPSUVREAE','google','Hi Lampo Team,<br><br>Hope everyone is well! I’ve got some feedback from our recent visit this past Sunday that I wanted to share with you all. We’ve always been big fans of Lampo’s pizza, but our last order from the IX Park location left us a bit puzzled.<br><br>We ordered a Margherita and a Hellboy (with pepperoni instead) and noticed that the dough was undercooked, not like the perfect crust we’re used to from Lampo. It''s not raw or cold, but warm and mushy.  The crust is not crispy on the bottom which is your style, but this time the final product missed maybe longer cook time or hotter temperature.<br><br>Also, the hot honey was missing its usual spicy kick and was thicker than what we’ve enjoyed before.<br><br>Spending $44 and not getting the usual awesome Lampo experience was disappointing. We really hope that the quality at the IX Park location jumps back to what we know and love soon!<br><br>However, until we''re sure the next time will be back to the top-notch Lampo standard, we might hold off on our next visit. We’re looking forward to seeing the awesome reviews roll in again and trying those perfect pizzas we miss.<br><br>Thanks for taking the time to read our thoughts, and we can’t wait to be back!<br><br>Best,<br>Kyle',4,'2023-10-03','2026-11-12T15:37:09.035Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('d235657a-1b34-401e-9441-8bf9b64cd8c7','3c59354c-78be-4335-ac27-a27ff4cce713','google:ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNaeE9QVXBRRRAB','google','I ordered the DOC Margarita pizza and it was so good I was genuinely sad when I finished it because the experience was over.<br><br>Crust: rich, flavorful, soft but crunchy, wonderfully chewy, but fewer air bubbles than I prefer.<br>Sauce: maybe the best pizza sauce I have ever had<br>Cheese: perfect flavor, but not enough.<br><br>As a general pizza I give it 🍕🍕🍕🍕🍕<br><br>Comparing it specifically to neopolitin pizza you could get in Italy or NYC I give it 🍕🍕🍕🍕',5,'2023-09-04','2026-11-12T15:37:09.035Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('2dba1e33-e5b4-473f-9a30-b8ed04d26074','3c59354c-78be-4335-ac27-a27ff4cce713','google:ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNaZ09QMXR3RRAB','google','Easy menu, easy to order, food is great but a little pricey. Expect to spend close to $20 a person. Only reason why I gave the atmosphere 1 star is because there is no atmosphere, it’s a pick up place so if you want to eat there you have to find your own space',5,'2023-09-01','2026-11-12T15:37:09.035Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('83e76785-859b-4109-a7d5-e9a1b0096dac','3c59354c-78be-4335-ac27-a27ff4cce713','google:ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURSNzliX1F3EAE','google','I order a pizza to pick up and when I get home I was surprised of the bad quality of this pizza.  Definitely I’m not going to order here anymore. The size and the price it’s ridiculous. You can see in the picture.',1,'2023-05-07','2026-11-12T15:37:09.035Z');
