INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('c299ce58-47fa-41f2-aa91-a47263a0eb81','5c968915-a2bc-4c16-853d-9cb76036347f','google:Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tsMldHRmxNR2xhU1VWblJUaGtSRVEwY0RFMmVWRRAB','google','Absolutely everything was fabulous. The service was amazing. The food light but filling. Authentic taste, flavors, textures.',5,'2026-08-22','2026-11-12T15:37:24.819Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('feb3ad76-ca29-44ac-99d3-d3afd5dd0f35','5c968915-a2bc-4c16-853d-9cb76036347f','google:Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT205SWQyRjFSbGRFUW1SdE1WaHVMVGQxUTBJelVsRRAB','google','The food was delicious and the staff were incredibly helpful and kind, explaining the menu to help my grandfather find gluten free options.',5,'2026-08-22','2026-11-12T15:37:24.819Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('3dd15947-15a4-4308-8e75-8e225fe0a2db','5c968915-a2bc-4c16-853d-9cb76036347f','google:Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2psT09UZG1SVlZPV2t4TFNrNXFaR3h4Y2trMWIzYxAB','google','Some restaurants survive on hype. Others survive because they quietly turn out great food day after day and build a loyal following one meal at a time. Thyme & Co in Charlottesville is the latter.<br><br>I''ve eaten my way through most of the menu at this point, and I can honestly say I haven''t been disappointed once.<br><br>The spicy hummus alone is worth the trip. It''s got just the right amount of heat, balanced with that smooth, rich texture that makes you keep reaching for another bite even when you tell yourself you''re done. The fresh manoussheh comes out warm and fragrant, tasting like something that was made for you, not assembled for you.<br><br>The beef shawarma is consistently excellent: tender, flavorful, and packed with the kind of seasoning that reminds you why shawarma has earned a place among the world''s great street foods. The kafta is equally impressive, perfectly seasoned and cooked with care. And then there''s the halloumi. Salty, rich, and grilled just right, it''s the kind of thing that makes you stop mid-conversation and appreciate what''s on your plate.<br><br>The falafel deserves a mention too. Crisp on the outside, light inside, and a world away from the dry hockey pucks that too many places try to pass off as falafel. The lamb is outstanding as well, full of flavor and always satisfying whether you''re getting it in a wrap or a bowl.<br><br>What makes the place even better is the people behind the counter. They''re genuinely friendly, welcoming, and seem happy to be there. After enough visits, you start to recognize familiar faces, and they recognize you. That kind of hospitality can''t be faked, and it''s becoming increasingly rare.<br><br>Thyme & Co doesn''t need gimmicks. It doesn''t need a flashy dining room or an elaborate sales pitch. It simply serves fresh, authentic Mediterranean and Lebanese food made with care by good people who clearly take pride in what they do.<br><br>In a town full of good food options, that''s enough to keep me coming back. And after working through most of the menu, I''m still looking forward to my next visit.',5,'2026-08-19','2026-11-12T15:37:24.819Z');
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO reviews VALUES('fd49e739-7894-4eff-8779-9dd67973f33a','5c968915-a2bc-4c16-853d-9cb76036347f','google:Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT21jMllqbFNORmQwVGtaeVNIWjJTRE5UUzJKUmNFRRAB','google','Hummus, gyros, and baklava were all excellent!',5,'2026-08-17','2026-11-12T15:37:24.819Z');
